#20100
Under the Eaves of the Hollow Wood~
   The burned trees of the Marches give way to living ones, tall and grey-
barked, their branches knitting overhead. The light turns dim and green. It
is very quiet; no birds, no insects, not even wind. The road runs on west,
narrowing to a track.
~
