#20102
The Woodcutters' Clearing~
   A clearing where woodcutters worked: stumps, stacked logs, a lean-to of
bark. Their axes are still buried in a half-felled tree. The tree is
bleeding a thick grey sap from the cut, and the sap has crept down the trunk
and across the ground toward the lean-to.
