The Webbed Thicket~
   Webs as thick as rope span the gaps between the trees, white and grey and
heavy with wrapped shapes. Some of the shapes are deer. Some are not. The
webs tremble constantly, though there is no wind, and the trembling grows
stronger as you go deeper.
