#20124
The Western Edge of the Wood~
   The trees thin out at last, and the track runs down a slope into low, wet
ground. The air changes, heavy with the smell of stagnant water and rot.
Ahead, mist hangs over the Greywater Fens, and somewhere out in it a bell is
tolling, slow and muffled.
